tonight we have a date for the return of  some ccsd  students and teachers back to the  classroom eight news now reporter orco  manon joining us live to explain the  timeline  and how parents are reacting orco  well if your kitchen table looks like  this you are not alone because of  distance learning  we have turned our homes into makeshift  schools but there is some good news  in just 33 days some ccsc students  are heading back to the classroom it's  definitely a relief  the clark county school district  announcing pre-k through third grade  students will begin hybrid learning on  march 1st that includes some  in-person instruction syrah valenzuela  tells me her two daughters in first and  third grade have been struggling with  distance education during covet 19  because they can't be with their  classmates at least just to  talk and to laugh and to joke around i  think  it you know they're really looking  forward to that ccsd  sending this memo to educators saying  they can return to the classroom on  february 22nd to prepare  kindergarten teacher kristen nigro is  ready it's a lot different when you have  the person in front of you rather than  looking through a computer screen  and so i think that it's going to really  help them focus but what about  other students ccsd says quote  throughout the second semester  the district will work to transition  additional grade levels to the hybrid  instructional model but education  advocates are concerned there's no  timeline yet the kids that are  having the most challenges from a mental  health perspective  are older students but right now we have  no plan for when those kids are going to  go back  but many like valenzuela agree this is a  good first step  now at least there's a little bit more  of a peace of mind  the district is asking parents to fill  out this online questionnaire by the end  of the day friday to help plan  for the pre-k through grade three  transition and you can find a link to  that on our website  8newsnow.com reporting live tonight orco  mana 8 news now
 

